Rust dependencies
-----------------
The Linux inventory in licenses/dependencies/INDEX.json records the active normal
and build dependencies, declared license expressions, authors, source locations
and checksums of collected notices. Each package has its own notice directory.
Pinned upstream notices supplement crates that omit license texts from their
published package. Their source revisions and checksums are recorded in
licenses/upstream/SOURCES.json. Source comment attributions are preserved where
present, including SPDX copyright headers.

The Rust standard library notices are included in
licenses/dependencies/rust/COPYRIGHT-library.html. The index records the compiler
version used to collect them. Native system libraries are supplied by the host;
they are not bundled by the user-local installer.

Regenerate after changing Cargo.lock or the compiler:
    python3 scripts/dependency_notices.py
Verify before packaging:
    python3 scripts/dependency_notices.py --check
These commands use the local Cargo cache with locked, offline resolution. The
inventory covers x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu by default; a different target requires
regeneration with --target and review of that target's native dependencies.
The installer includes this entire licenses directory. Collection preserves
upstream notices; it does not certify license compatibility or cover libraries
added by an external packaging system.

